Here we recognize the property of fractions, i.e., 
\[
  \frac{1}{a} 
    = \frac{b}{ab}
 = \frac{c}{ac}
\]
and 
\[
  \frac{1}{a} - \frac{1}{b}
  = \frac{b}{ab} - \frac{a}{ab}
  = \frac{b - a}{ab}.
\]
Hence
\[
  \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13}
   = \frac{13 - 11}{13 \times 11}
 = \frac{2}{143} \, .
\]
Due to the symmetry, it is also the case that
\[
  \frac{1}{13} - \frac{1}{17}
   = \frac{17 - 13}{17 \times 13}
 = \frac{4}{221} \, .
\]
With similar reasoning for the remaining terms, 
we know that
\[
  \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13}
   = \frac{17 - 13}{17 \times 13}
 = \frac{4}{221} \, ,
\]
\[
  \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{11}
   = \frac{11 - 17}{11 \times 17}
 = -\frac{6}{187} \, ,
\]
and
\[
  \frac{1}{11} - \frac{1}{13}
   = \frac{17 - 13}{17 \times 13}
 = \frac{4}{221} \, .
\]
Combined with this, the expression becomes
\[
  \frac{121 \left( \frac{4}{221} \right)
        + 169 \left( -\frac{6}{187} \right) 
        + 289 \left( \frac{2}{143} \right)}{
        11 \left( \frac{4}{221} \right)
        + 13 \left( -\frac{6}{187} \right)
        + 17 \left( \frac{2}{143} \right)} \, .
\]
By simplifying the fractions and applying basic algebra, 
we obtain
\[
  \frac{484}{2756}
  = \frac{4}{11}
  = \frac{3874}{9991} \, .
\]
<answer>
  \(\frac{3874}{9991}\)

